1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,370
Listen. Practice. Speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:12,370 --> 00:00:17,360
Good morning. Glad we could finally sit down today.

3
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:24,360
I know the last few weeks have been packed with campaign reviews, product demos, and the Q4 content planning rush,

4
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:29,360
but carving out time for this marketing strategy discussion is long overdue.

5
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:32,360
Absolutely. And good morning to you as well.

6
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:38,040
Well, the digital team has been running non-stop with analytics updates and performance reports,

7
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,160
and the creative team is already asking for clarity on next quarter's direction.

8
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:46,480
So yes, this conversation needs to happen now before we fall behind the curve.

9
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:47,600
Exactly.

10
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,600
Marketing is moving too fast these days.

11
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:55,520
Algorithms shift overnight, consumer behavior is evolving every week, and competition is

12
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:58,920
becoming more aggressive across every channel.

13
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:04,360
That's why today, I'd like us to revisit our positioning, revise our content strategy,

14
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:07,520
and take a hard look at what's working and what's not.

15
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:08,800
That sounds like a plan.

16
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:12,080
To get started, maybe we should analyze the current situation.

17
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:17,440
If you look at the last three months, we saw solid traffic growth about 18%, but conversion

18
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:18,960
rates stayed flat.

19
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:22,680
That suggests interest is growing, but the value proposition isn't strong enough

20
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:24,640
to push people to take action.

21
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:25,640
Right.

22
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:28,840
I've noticed the same thing across multiple touch points.

23
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:32,600
We're attracting leads, but we're not compelling them strongly enough.

24
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:37,360
The funnel is filling up, but too many people drop out during the middle stages.

25
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:40,600
It's a classic awareness without engagement issue.

26
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:43,800
Exactly, and our messaging might be part of the problem.

27
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:47,400
If you look across our ads, social posts, landing pages and

28
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:50,760
email sequences, the tone is not always consistent.

29
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:54,360
Sometimes we sound premium, sometimes we sound budget friendly.

30
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,480
Sometimes we sound overly corporate.

31
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:58,360
We need one unified voice.

32
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:00,880
Yes, brand voice is crucial.

33
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:03,760
Consumers don't trust inconsistent brands.

34
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,600
They trust familiarity.

35
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,160
And in marketing, familiarity is everything.

36
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:11,240
Our messaging needs to feel aligned

37
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,520
no matter where customers encounter us.

38
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,560
TikTok, LinkedIn, YouTube, the website,

39
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:18,560
or even an email newsletter.

40
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:19,400
I agree.

41
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:22,560
And about platforms, our performance varies dramatically

42
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:23,480
across them.

43
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:27,380
TikTok is generating reach, but almost no qualified leads.

44
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:29,460
LinkedIn is generating high quality leads,

45
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:30,780
but at a higher cost.

46
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:32,720
YouTube ads show great retention,

47
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:35,040
but watch to click conversion is weak.

48
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:37,380
The ecosystem feels fragmented.

49
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:39,900
True, but fragmentation can be managed

50
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,020
with a strong funnel strategy.

51
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:45,620
We need to use each platform for its natural strengths.

52
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:49,220
TikTok for quick awareness, Instagram for storytelling,

53
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:51,380
YouTube for educational depth,

54
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:55,720
LinkedIn for B2B authority, and email for nurturing.

55
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,800
It's about assigning the right job to the right platform.

56
00:02:58,800 --> 00:02:59,720
Exactly.

57
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:01,840
And speaking of email, our open rates

58
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,720
and click-through rates have been dropping,

59
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:06,720
not dramatically, but enough to be concerning.

60
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:08,480
I think the issue is that our newsletters

61
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:10,560
became too promotional.

62
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,720
People don't want constant sales pitches,

63
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:14,320
they want value.

64
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:16,640
We need to reintroduce educational content

65
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:18,440
that solves real problems.

66
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:21,780
Yes, value first, pitch later.

67
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:24,000
That's how modern marketing works,

68
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,720
and we need to remember something important.

69
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:29,480
Today's consumers are incredibly smart.

70
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:32,560
They can smell a sales tactic from a mile away.

71
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:36,040
So our approach needs to shift from sell this product

72
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:38,120
to understand this need,

73
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:41,400
then show how our product naturally fits.

74
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:43,200
That's how trust is built.

75
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,840
Agreed, and trust is everything,

76
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:48,200
especially now when buyers are overwhelmed

77
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:53,960
choices. If we want loyalty, we need to create emotional resonance, not just information.

78
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:56,520
Storytelling should play a bigger role in our campaigns.

79
00:03:56,520 --> 00:04:02,440
Absolutely. Stories sell more effectively than features. Humans connect with narratives.

80
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:08,760
Instead of saying our product is fast, we should tell a story about someone whose life got easier

81
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:14,120
because of that speed. That's the difference between content people scroll past and content

82
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:19,560
people remember. Exactly. And I think our creative team is talented enough to execute that,

83
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:23,800
if we give them clearer direction. Right now, they're producing great visuals,

84
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:28,840
but the emotional angle is missing. We need to brief them with deeper insights into customer

85
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:34,760
pain points, not just product specs. Insight driven creativity is always more impactful.

86
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:40,600
Yes. And that brings up the next point, market research. We have some data, but not enough.

87
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:49,600
Our personas are to surface level. We know demographics and job titles, but we don't know beliefs, motivations, fears, or decision triggers.

88
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:53,600
Without psychological insight, marketing becomes guesswork.

89
00:04:53,600 --> 00:05:00,600
Exactly. And guesswork is expensive. We need a richer understanding of what truly influences our buyers.

90
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:06,600
For example, why do some leads hesitate to book a demo? Why do some customers drop off after the trial phase?

91
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:09,720
Why do some others upgrade quickly?

92
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:12,360
These patterns hold the key to our future strategy.

93
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,360
Right.

94
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:18,040
Maybe we should run more surveys, customer interviews, and even social listening.

95
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,760
People say a lot online.

96
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:23,040
Complaints, praise, confusion, expectations.

97
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:27,280
If we analyze these conversations, we'll understand how our brand fits into the

98
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:28,880
broader market.

99
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:32,600
Once we know how people talk about us, we'll know how to talk to them.

100
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,600
Yes.

101
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:37,220
We're on the topic of feedback, let's discuss user-generated content.

102
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:39,720
We're not leveraging it nearly enough.

103
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:44,520
Customers love authenticity, and nothing is more authentic than real users showing real

104
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,720
experiences.

105
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,560
It builds trust instantly.

106
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:48,920
I agree.

107
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:53,360
And UGC is cheaper, more organic, and more persuasive than Poly.

108
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:54,840
Good morning.

109
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:56,360
Thanks for meeting with me today.

110
00:05:56,360 --> 00:06:01,460
I know your schedule has been absolutely overloaded, especially with all the moving

111
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:08,500
parts around the upcoming rebranding discussions, but I think this conversation is overdue.

112
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:14,700
We've been circling around the same issues for weeks, mentioning ideas and passing, but

113
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:18,900
we haven't had a focused, comprehensive dialogue.

114
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:24,700
And given the pressure we're under, from leadership, from competitors and from customers, we really

115
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:26,580
need clarity.

116
00:06:26,580 --> 00:06:28,700
So let's jump into it.

117
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:31,980
How are you feeling about where things stand?

118
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:32,980
Good morning.

119
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:34,060
I agree.

120
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:36,850
We really needed this meeting.

121
00:06:36,850 --> 00:06:42,050
To be honest, I'd been feeling a bit conflicted about the brand direction.

122
00:06:42,050 --> 00:06:46,890
Not in a negative way, but there's this sense that our identity is shifting faster

123
00:06:46,890 --> 00:06:48,330
than our messaging.

124
00:06:48,330 --> 00:06:53,010
And our messaging is shifting faster than our actual customer perception.

125
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:54,770
There's a gap forming.

126
00:06:54,770 --> 00:07:00,790
And if we don't align soon, the market is going to define our brand for us rather than

127
00:07:00,790 --> 00:07:02,880
us defining it.

128
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,880
That's never a good place to be.

129
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:10,120
So yes, I'm glad we're talking about positioning and what the rebrand should truly reflect.

130
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,320
Exactly.

131
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:13,440
And that's the core of the issue.

132
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:16,360
The brand can't just look better.

133
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:18,040
It has to mean something.

134
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:22,600
It has to be aligned with who we are, where we're going, and what our customers

135
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,840
expect from us.

136
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:30,120
Over the past few months, I've had multiple conversations with customers, sales teams,

137
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:34,720
and even external partners, and I'm noticing the same pattern.

138
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:41,200
People know what we do, but they don't necessarily know what we stand for.

139
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:45,640
That's a risky position for any business, especially in a crowded market.

140
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:48,180
I've been hearing the same thing.

141
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:52,720
People recognize our service offering, they're aware of our products, and they trust

142
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:57,400
our capabilities, but emotionally, the brand doesn't connect.

143
00:07:57,400 --> 00:08:00,920
It's functional, rational, and transactional.

144
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:07,080
But brands that grow, brands that scale, are brands that build emotional resonance.

145
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:11,040
It's not enough for customers to think they deliver good services.

146
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:14,160
They have to think, this brand aligns with my values.

147
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,920
This brand understands me.

148
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:18,020
And currently, I don't think we're there.

149
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:19,660
No, we're not.

150
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:25,300
And what surprises me is that our culture internally is much stronger than our external

151
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:26,700
identity.

152
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:31,660
Employees feel proud, they feel connected, they collaborate well.

153
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:35,580
But that sense of purpose and energy doesn't translate outwards.

154
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:39,100
If anything, our external brand materials feel dated.

155
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:45,340
The visuals are old-fashioned, the messaging is vague, the tone of voice feels corporate,

156
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:46,500
not human.

157
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:51,700
And in a market that values authenticity, that's not going to work anymore.

158
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:53,020
Absolutely.

159
00:08:53,020 --> 00:08:56,940
Our tone is polite, professional, but flat.

160
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:58,660
It doesn't inspire.

161
00:08:58,660 --> 00:08:59,660
It doesn't challenge.

162
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:01,220
It doesn't differentiate.

163
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:05,220
And differentiation is what positioning is all about.

164
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:07,900
That brings me to something I wanted to ask you.

165
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:12,780
In your view, who do you think we really are as a brand?

166
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:18,320
Not the standard mission statement, not the corporate jargon, but the authentic identity

167
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,660
at the core.

168
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:22,020
That's a good question.

169
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:27,140
I think at our core, we're a brand that stands for progress.

170
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:31,460
We help customers improve, grow, adapt, and succeed.

171
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:36,420
Whether it's through our technology or our services, we're essentially an enabler

172
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:38,460
of transformation.

173
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:41,500
But we never articulate that clearly.

174
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:45,420
Instead, we talk about features, pricing, and performance metrics.

175
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:51,660
Meanwhile, our competitors talk about vision, innovation, empowerment, and identity.

176
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:56,540
They're owning the emotional space while we're stuck in the rational lane.

177
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:58,580
That's exactly how I see it too.

178
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:00,140
And the funny thing is, you're right.

179
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:03,140
Our internal culture embodies transformation.

180
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:07,140
We're always innovating, always improving, always moving.

181
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:11,940
But we communicate like a conservative, slow-paced, risk-averse brand.

182
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:16,820
The gap between who we are and who we sound like is getting bigger, and that gap is what

183
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:19,500
the rebranding must solve.

184
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:21,460
But here's the challenge.

185
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:24,460
Rebranding cannot just be about changing logos and colors.

186
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:26,380
It has to start with positioning.

187
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:27,700
Yes.

188
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:31,140
Positioning first, identity second.

189
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:35,420
And positioning must answer simple but powerful questions.

190
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:37,260
What makes us different?

191
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:39,540
Why do customers choose us?

192
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:42,380
Why should they choose us in the future?

193
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:46,520
What role do we play in their lives or businesses?

194
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:51,180
What value do we deliver that no one else can?

195
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:55,900
And I think we haven't clearly defined those answers in years.

196
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:59,500
Honestly, I think we've never defined them properly.

197
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:05,220
We've always had broad statements like, we deliver quality, or we focus on customer

198
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:08,700
or satisfaction, but those aren't differentiators.

199
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:12,450
They're expectations, they're table stakes.

200
00:11:12,450 --> 00:11:16,010
If we want a strong position, we need something bold,

201
00:11:16,010 --> 00:11:19,450
something meaningful, something that makes a customer

202
00:11:19,450 --> 00:11:21,710
instantly understand not only the function

203
00:11:21,710 --> 00:11:24,050
of what we offer.

204
00:11:24,050 --> 00:11:25,170
Good morning.

205
00:11:25,170 --> 00:11:27,090
Thanks for joining me early today.

206
00:11:27,090 --> 00:11:29,530
I know everyone is busy with the campaigns

207
00:11:29,530 --> 00:11:32,090
lined up for this quarter, and I appreciate you

208
00:11:32,090 --> 00:11:33,770
making time for a deep dive

209
00:11:33,770 --> 00:11:36,330
into the overall marketing strategy.

210
00:11:36,330 --> 00:11:38,090
We've been moving fast lately,

211
00:11:38,090 --> 00:11:40,570
but I feel we need a stronger alignment

212
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:42,610
to ensure our next campaigns land

213
00:11:42,610 --> 00:11:44,770
exactly the way we intend.

214
00:11:44,770 --> 00:11:46,490
Absolutely, I agree.

215
00:11:46,490 --> 00:11:48,610
There's so much happening at once.

216
00:11:48,610 --> 00:11:51,970
Content creation, digital ads, product launches,

217
00:11:51,970 --> 00:11:54,650
brand collaborations, influencer outreach,

218
00:11:54,650 --> 00:11:56,730
customer research, you name it.

219
00:11:56,730 --> 00:12:00,170
And everything feels like it's happening at full speed.

220
00:12:00,170 --> 00:12:02,650
I think it's the perfect time to pause,

221
00:12:02,650 --> 00:12:04,810
reflect and align.

222
00:12:04,810 --> 00:12:06,370
The market is shifting quickly

223
00:12:06,370 --> 00:12:09,870
and consumer attention spans are shorter than ever.

224
00:12:09,870 --> 00:12:11,690
If we don't act strategically,

225
00:12:11,690 --> 00:12:13,450
our message will get lost.

226
00:12:13,450 --> 00:12:14,690
Exactly.

227
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:17,570
The competitive landscape is changing dramatically.

228
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:20,250
New players are entering almost every month

229
00:12:20,250 --> 00:12:23,090
and they're using aggressive digital strategies.

230
00:12:23,090 --> 00:12:25,170
Some brands are capturing market share

231
00:12:25,170 --> 00:12:27,310
not because their product is better

232
00:12:27,310 --> 00:12:30,210
but because their storytelling is more compelling.

233
00:12:30,210 --> 00:12:32,050
That's what I want us to address.

234
00:12:32,050 --> 00:12:38,210
storytelling, customer engagement, emotional connection, and digital consistency. These

235
00:12:38,210 --> 00:12:44,530
need to become our strengths. I completely agree. One of the challenges I've observed is that

236
00:12:44,530 --> 00:12:50,610
although we have strong products and a well-established brand identity, our messaging is not always

237
00:12:50,610 --> 00:12:55,970
cohesive across platforms. What we say on our digital ads isn't always aligned with what we

238
00:12:55,970 --> 00:13:00,290
say on our socials, and what we say on our socials doesn't always match the tone of our

239
00:13:00,290 --> 00:13:05,890
website, the customer journey becomes fragmented, and that creates confusion.

240
00:13:05,890 --> 00:13:11,090
Yes, and that inconsistency weakens brand recall.

241
00:13:11,090 --> 00:13:15,570
When customers see an ad, then see a post, then visit our website.

242
00:13:15,570 --> 00:13:21,670
Each touch point should reinforce the same promise, the same tone, the same personality.

243
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:27,170
Marketing today is not about one big campaign, it's about repeating one strong message

244
00:13:27,170 --> 00:13:34,250
across dozens of channels, so customers deeply internalize who we are and why we matter.

245
00:13:34,250 --> 00:13:35,250
Exactly.

246
00:13:35,250 --> 00:13:39,810
And that's why one of the things I want to emphasize today is unified branding, unified

247
00:13:39,810 --> 00:13:46,630
language, unified style, unified visuals, but more importantly, unified intent.

248
00:13:46,630 --> 00:13:48,690
That's what we need at this stage.

249
00:13:48,690 --> 00:13:50,030
Absolutely.

250
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:52,490
But let's start with the big picture.

251
00:13:52,490 --> 00:13:57,970
Our marketing for the next 12 months can be summarized into four key goals.

252
00:13:57,970 --> 00:14:03,930
Stronger brand awareness, higher digital engagement, improved conversion rates, and deeper customer

253
00:14:03,930 --> 00:14:04,930
loyalty.

254
00:14:04,930 --> 00:14:10,250
